(* VimMotions — battallion's keymap: vim's normal-mode grammar, and the insert, replace, command
 * and help modes.
 *
 * A plugin. It imports `Api` for the state operations, `Key` for the key values, and the three
 * modules that answer where a motion lands (Motions.trp), what text an object names
 * (TextObjects.trp) and what an operator does to a range (Operators.trp). It holds no authority,
 * no pid and no descriptor, and its whole effect on the editor is the state it returns. The kernel
 * hands it the `api` record, a command interpreter and the help page count, and folds its `onKey`
 * over the decoded keys.
 *
 * ONE KEY IN, ONE STATE OUT. `onKey (api, commands, helpPages, st, k)` returns `(state', quit)`;
 * `quit` is true when the key ends the session. A key that asks for something the kernel must do
 * — a write — leaves a request in the state instead (`api.requestWrite`), which the kernel carries
 * out before folding the keys behind it.
 *
 * THE COMMAND WORD IS NOT THIS PLUGIN'S. `:` opens the command line and this module edits it, but
 * what a command *means* is FileOps.trp's: on Enter the line is handed to the `commands` function
 * the kernel passed in, with the mode already back to normal and the line cleared. `q`, CTRL-c
 * and `ZQ` go through the same function as the words "q" and "q!", and `ZZ` as "wq", which is
 * what makes them behave exactly as the typed commands do.
 *
 * A KEY IS A TOKEN. Every key is turned into a string first: a printable key is its own
 * character, and every other key a name in angle brackets — `<enter>`, `<down>`, `<c-r>`. The
 * grammar below is written over tokens, so `d<down>` and `dj` are the same command, and the keys
 * typed in an insert are kept as tokens and replayed as tokens.
 *
 * NORMAL MODE IS A GRAMMAR, NOT A LIST OF BINDINGS:
 *
 *     [count] operator [count] (motion | text object | operator again)
 *     [count] command
 *
 * `st.pending` is the printable tokens of the command typed so far, shown at the end of the
 * status line. Each key extends it and the whole is parsed again: a complete command runs and
 * clears it, an incomplete one keeps it, and a sequence the grammar has no reading for drops it
 * — so `d` then `x` does nothing and leaves normal mode where it was, Esc abandons whatever is
 * pending, and no key is ever left half-pressed. A named key never stays pending: it completes a
 * command or it cancels one. Two counts multiply: `2d3w` deletes six words.
 *
 * THE OPERATORS are `d` delete, `c` change, `y` yank, `<` and `>` shift, `g~`, `gu` and `gU`
 * for case. Doubled — `dd`, `yy`, `>>`, `gUU` — an operator takes the line, or `count` lines. THE
 * MOTIONS are `h j k l w W b B e E ge gE 0 ^ $ | f t F T ; , % { } gg G H M L + - _ n N * # '
 * \`` and the named keys; what each one means is Motions.trp's, and whether the text it covers
 * ends before or on the character it lands on — exclusive, inclusive or linewise — is the table
 * `kindOf` below. THE TEXT OBJECTS are `i` or `a` with `w W ( ) b [ ] { } B < > " ' \` p`. THE
 * COMMANDS are the keys that stand alone: `x X s S D C Y p P J gJ r ~ u CTRL-r . i a I A o O R m
 * zz zt zb ZZ ZQ : / ? q CTRL-c CTRL-e CTRL-y CTRL-d CTRL-u CTRL-f CTRL-b`. `q` quits rather than
 * recording a macro: there are no registers to record into, and the editor has had `q` for quit
 * since it could quit.
 *
 * A MOTION THAT CANNOT BE MADE ABORTS ITS COMMAND. `fx` on a line without an `x`, `j` on the last
 * line, `e` at the end of the buffer: the motion answers NONE, the command does nothing and the
 * state is what it was. Under an operator that is what keeps `dfx` from deleting anything when
 * there is no `x`.
 *
 * THE CURSOR IS ON A CHARACTER IN NORMAL MODE, as vi's is: after every normal-mode command
 * `api.intoLine` pulls a cursor that sits past the last character back onto it, and leaving
 * insert mode steps the cursor left by one. Insert mode may sit past the end, since that is where
 * appended text goes; `a` and `A` are the keys that put it there. The goal column is not touched
 * by the pull, so `$` and then `j` still walk down the ends of the lines.
 *
 * EVERY COMMAND IS ONE UNDO STEP, and so is every insert. A command that edits several times —
 * `3x`, `J`, `>j` — pushes several undo entries and squashes them into one when it completes; an
 * insert notes the undo depth when it begins and squashes when Esc ends it (Api.trp's
 * `beginInsert` and `endInsert`). A change that opens an insert, `cw` or `o`, begins the insert
 * before it edits, so that the deletion and the typing are one step too.
 *
 * `.` REPEATS THE LAST CHANGE. When a change completes, its tokens are kept (`st.dot`), and when
 * it opened an insert the keys typed until Esc are kept beside them (`st.dotInsert`). `.` runs
 * the tokens again and then types the keys again; a count given to `.` replaces the count that
 * was recorded. A count on an insert command — `3ix`, `2o` — repeats the typed keys, or for `o`
 * and `O` the whole command, that many times when Esc is pressed, which is the same replay.
 *
 * THE REGISTER IS ONE, THE UNNAMED. Everything that deletes writes it — `x`, `dw`, `dd`, `s`,
 * `C` — and `y` writes it without deleting; the text is marked charwise or linewise, and `p` and
 * `P` put it accordingly, `count` times. There are no named registers.
 *
 * REPLACE MODE overwrites: a printable key replaces the character under the cursor and moves on,
 * or appends past the end of the line; Backspace steps back and restores the character it had
 * overwritten, by undoing that one replacement; Enter breaks the line without replacing anything.
 * Everything else is insert mode's.
 *
 * COMMAND MODE IS ONE MODE FOR THREE PROMPTS. `:` opens it with a colon, `/` and `?` with the
 * search's direction, and `st.prompt` is which. The editing is the same for all — printable keys
 * extend the line, Backspace shortens it and leaves the mode when the line is empty, as
 * backspacing over the colon does in vi, Esc cancels — and only Enter looks at the prompt, handing
 * a colon line to the command interpreter and a search line to the search.
 *
 * MARKS ARE POSITIONS. `m` with a letter notes the cursor, `'` with the letter goes to the first
 * non-blank of its line and `` ` `` to the exact column, both clamped to the buffer as it now
 * stands: an edit above a mark does not move it. `''` and ``` `` ``` go back to where the cursor
 * was before the last jump — a jump being any of `G gg % { } n N * # H M L` or a search, or a
 * mark.
 *
 * THE LINEWISE KEYS LAND ON THE FIRST NON-BLANK, as vim's do with `startofline` set: `gg`, `G`,
 * `dd`, `j` after a linewise put, `'a`.
 *)

import String
import List
import Option
import "./Api"
import "./Key"
import "./Motions"
import "./TextObjects"
import "./Operators"

(* What an operator is applied to. *)
datatype target = MOTION of string * string     (* the motion's name and its character, if any *)
                | OBJECT of string * string     (* "i" or "a", and the object's character      *)
                | SAME                          (* the operator doubled: the line               *)

(* A complete normal-mode command: an operator with its target, or a command that stands alone,
 * each with the count typed before it, if one was. *)
datatype cmd = OPERATE of int option * string * target
             | ACT     of int option * string * string

datatype outcome = DONE of cmd | MORE | BAD

let (*-----------------------------------  Messages  ----------------------------------*)

    val noPatternMessage = "no previous search pattern"
    val noMarkMessage    = "mark not set"
    val noChangeMessage  = "no change to repeat"

    (*------------------------------------  Tokens  -----------------------------------*)

    fun tokenOf (KEY_PRINT c)   = c
      | tokenOf KEY_ENTER       = "<enter>"
      | tokenOf KEY_TAB         = "<tab>"
      | tokenOf KEY_BACKSPACE   = "<bs>"
      | tokenOf KEY_DELETE      = "<del>"
      | tokenOf KEY_ESC         = "<esc>"
      | tokenOf KEY_UP          = "<up>"
      | tokenOf KEY_DOWN        = "<down>"
      | tokenOf KEY_LEFT        = "<left>"
      | tokenOf KEY_RIGHT       = "<right>"
      | tokenOf KEY_HOME        = "<home>"
      | tokenOf KEY_END         = "<end>"
      | tokenOf KEY_PAGEUP      = "<pgup>"
      | tokenOf KEY_PAGEDOWN    = "<pgdn>"
      | tokenOf (KEY_CTRL c)    = "<c-" ^ c ^ ">"
      | tokenOf (KEY_UNKNOWN s) = "<?>"

    (** Whether a token is a printable key: one code point, which is not a name. *)
    fun isPrintable t = String.size t = 1 orelse (String.size t = 2 andalso String.sub (t, 0) <> "<")

    (** The tokens of a pending string: its code points, a surrogate pair kept together. *)
    fun tokensOf s =
        let val n = String.size s
            fun go (i, acc) =
                if i >= n then List.reverse acc
                else let val u = String.subCode (s, i)
                         val w = if u >= 0xd800 andalso u <= 0xdbff andalso i + 1 < n then 2 else 1
                     in go (i + w, String.substring (s, i, i + w) :: acc)
                     end
        in go (0, [])
        end

    fun isDigit t = String.size t = 1 andalso String.subCode (t, 0) >= 48 andalso String.subCode (t, 0) <= 57

    fun digitOf t = String.subCode (t, 0) - 48

    fun isLetter t = String.size t = 1 andalso String.subCode (t, 0) >= 97 andalso String.subCode (t, 0) <= 122

    (*----------------------------------  The grammar  ---------------------------------*)

    (** A count: digits starting with one that is not `0`, `0` alone being the motion. *)
    fun count toks =
        let fun go (t :: rest, n) = if isDigit t then go (rest, n * 10 + digitOf t)
                                    else (SOME n, t :: rest)
              | go ([], n)        = (SOME n, [])
        in case toks of
                t :: rest => if isDigit t andalso t <> "0" then go (rest, digitOf t)
                             else (NONE, toks)
              | []        => (NONE, [])
        end

    fun mul (SOME a, SOME b) = SOME (a * b)
      | mul (SOME a, NONE)   = SOME a
      | mul (NONE, b)        = b

    fun isOperator t = t = "d" orelse t = "c" orelse t = "y" orelse t = "<" orelse t = ">"

    (** The token that doubles an operator: `dd`, `>>`, `gUU`. *)
    fun doubles ("g~", t) = t = "~"
      | doubles ("gu", t) = t = "u"
      | doubles ("gU", t) = t = "U"
      | doubles (op, t)   = t = op

    (** The motions that take a character. *)
    fun needsChar t = t = "f" orelse t = "t" orelse t = "F" orelse t = "T"
                      orelse t = "'" orelse t = "`"

    (** The one-token motions. *)
    fun isMotion t =
        List.elem t [ "h", "j", "k", "l", "w", "W", "b", "B", "e", "E", "0", "^", "$", "|"
                    , ";", ",", "%", "{", "}", "G", "H", "M", "L", "+", "-", "_", "n", "N"
                    , "*", "#", " ", "<left>", "<right>", "<up>", "<down>", "<home>", "<end>"
                    , "<bs>", "<enter>", "<pgup>", "<pgdn>", "<c-f>", "<c-b>", "<c-d>", "<c-u>" ]

    fun isObjectChar t =
        List.elem t [ "w", "W", "(", ")", "b", "[", "]", "{", "}", "B", "<", ">", "p"
                    , String.strCode 34, "'", "`" ]

    (** The commands that stand alone. *)
    fun isAct t =
        List.elem t [ "x", "X", "s", "S", "D", "C", "Y", "p", "P", "J", "~", "u", "."
                    , "i", "a", "I", "A", "o", "O", "R", ":", "/", "?", "q", "<del>"
                    , "<c-r>", "<c-c>", "<c-e>", "<c-y>", "<esc>", "v", "V" ]

    (** The rest of an operator's command: its own count and its target. *)
    fun parseTarget (n1, op, toks) =
        let val (n2, rest) = count toks
            val n = mul (n1, n2)
        in case rest of
                []        => MORE
              | t :: more =>
                  if doubles (op, t) then DONE (OPERATE (n, op, SAME))
                  else if t = "i" orelse t = "a"
                  then (case more of
                             []     => MORE
                           | u :: _ => if isObjectChar u then DONE (OPERATE (n, op, OBJECT (t, u)))
                                       else BAD)
                  else if t = "g"
                  then (case more of
                             []     => MORE
                           | u :: _ => if u = "g" orelse u = "e" orelse u = "E"
                                       then DONE (OPERATE (n, op, MOTION ("g" ^ u, "")))
                                       else if doubles (op, "g" ^ u) then DONE (OPERATE (n, op, SAME))
                                       else BAD)
                  else if needsChar t
                  then (case more of
                             []     => MORE
                           | u :: _ => DONE (OPERATE (n, op, MOTION (t, u))))
                  else if isMotion t then DONE (OPERATE (n, op, MOTION (t, "")))
                  else BAD
        end

    (** The tokens as a command: complete, incomplete, or nothing the grammar reads. *)
    fun parse toks =
        let val (n1, rest) = count toks
        in case rest of
                []        => MORE
              | t :: more =>
                  if isOperator t then parseTarget (n1, t, more)
                  else if t = "g"
                  then (case more of
                             []     => MORE
                           | u :: after =>
                               if u = "~" orelse u = "u" orelse u = "U" then parseTarget (n1, "g" ^ u, after)
                               else if u = "g" orelse u = "e" orelse u = "E" orelse u = "J"
                               then DONE (ACT (n1, "g" ^ u, ""))
                               else BAD)
                  else if t = "z" orelse t = "Z"
                  then (case more of
                             []     => MORE
                           | u :: _ => if (t = "z" andalso (u = "z" orelse u = "t" orelse u = "b"))
                                          orelse (t = "Z" andalso (u = "Z" orelse u = "Q"))
                                       then DONE (ACT (n1, t ^ u, "")) else BAD)
                  else if needsChar t orelse t = "r" orelse t = "m"
                  then (case more of
                             []     => MORE
                           | u :: _ => DONE (ACT (n1, t, u)))
                  else if isMotion t orelse isAct t then DONE (ACT (n1, t, ""))
                  else BAD
        end

    (*-----------------------------------  Motions  -----------------------------------*)

    (** How the text a motion covers is bounded. `;` and `,` take the kind of the find they
     *  repeat. *)
    fun kindOf (name, st) =
        if List.elem name ["j", "k", "<up>", "<down>", "gg", "G", "+", "-", "_", "<enter>"
                          , "H", "M", "L", "'", "<c-f>", "<c-b>", "<c-d>", "<c-u>", "<pgup>", "<pgdn>"]
        then LINEWISE
        else if List.elem name ["e", "E", "ge", "gE", "f", "t", "$", "<end>", "%"] then INCLUSIVE
        else if name = ";" orelse name = ","
        then (if String.size st.charFind > 0
                 andalso (String.sub (st.charFind, 0) = "f" orelse String.sub (st.charFind, 0) = "t")
              then INCLUSIVE else EXCLUSIVE)
        else EXCLUSIVE

    fun isJump name =
        List.elem name ["G", "gg", "%", "{", "}", "n", "N", "*", "#", "H", "M", "L", "'", "`"]

    fun nonBlank (api, st, l) = api.moveTo (st, l, Motions.firstNonBlank (api, st, l))

    (** The line `delta` lines away, at the goal column; NONE when the cursor cannot move that
     *  way at all. *)
    fun byLines (api, st, delta) =
        if (delta > 0 andalso st.line >= api.lastLine st) orelse (delta < 0 andalso st.line = 0)
        then NONE else SOME (api.moveLine (st, st.line + delta))

    (** The `;` and `,` repeat of the last character find, `count` times. *)
    fun repeatFind (api, st, reverse, n) =
        if String.size st.charFind < 2 then NONE
        else let val c0 = String.sub (st.charFind, 0)
                 val ch = String.substring (st.charFind, 1, String.size st.charFind)
                 val c1 = if not reverse then c0
                          else if c0 = "f" then "F" else if c0 = "F" then "f"
                          else if c0 = "t" then "T" else "t"
             in Motions.charFind (api, st, c1, ch, n, true)
             end

    (** `w` and `W` under an operator stop at the end of the line the last word moved over ends
     *  on, so that `dw` on the last word of a line does not join the next line onto it. *)
    fun wordForOp (api, st, n, big) =
        case Motions.wordForward (api, st, n, big) of
             NONE => NONE
           | SOME s =>
               if s.line = st.line then SOME s
               else let val prev = if n <= 1 then SOME st else Motions.wordForward (api, st, n - 1, big)
                    in case prev of
                            NONE => SOME s
                          | SOME p => if p.line < s.line
                                      then SOME (api.moveTo (st, p.line, api.lineLength (st, p.line)))
                                      else SOME s
                    end

    (** Where a motion lands: SOME state with the cursor there, or NONE. `forOp` says an operator
     *  is asking, in which case `l` may land past the end of the line and `w` stops at it. *)
    fun move (api, st, name, arg, cnt, forOp) =
        let val n = Option.getOrElse cnt 1
            val len = api.lineLength (st, st.line)
            val last = api.lastLine st
            val h = api.textRows st
        in      if name = "h" orelse name = "<left>" orelse name = "<bs>"
                then (if st.col = 0 then NONE else SOME (api.moveTo (st, st.line, st.col - n)))
           else if name = "l" orelse name = "<right>" orelse name = " "
                then (if forOp
                      then (if st.col >= len then NONE else SOME (api.moveTo (st, st.line, st.col + n)))
                      else if st.col + 1 >= len then NONE
                      else SOME (api.moveTo (st, st.line, if st.col + n >= len then len - 1 else st.col + n)))
           else if name = "j" orelse name = "<down>" then byLines (api, st, n)
           else if name = "k" orelse name = "<up>"   then byLines (api, st, 0 - n)
           else if name = "0" orelse name = "<home>" then SOME (api.moveTo (st, st.line, 0))
           else if name = "^" then SOME (nonBlank (api, st, st.line))
           else if name = "$" orelse name = "<end>"
                then (if st.line + n - 1 > last then NONE else SOME (api.moveEnd (st, st.line + n - 1)))
           else if name = "|" then SOME (api.moveTo (st, st.line, n - 1))
           else if name = "w" orelse name = "W"
                then (if forOp then wordForOp (api, st, n, name = "W")
                      else Motions.wordForward (api, st, n, name = "W"))
           else if name = "b" orelse name = "B" then Motions.wordBackward (api, st, n, name = "B")
           else if name = "e" orelse name = "E" then Motions.wordEnd (api, st, n, name = "E")
           else if name = "ge" orelse name = "gE" then Motions.wordEndBack (api, st, n, name = "gE")
           else if needsChar name andalso name <> "'" andalso name <> "`"
                then (if isPrintable arg
                      then Option.map (fn s => api.setCharFind (s, name ^ arg))
                                      (Motions.charFind (api, st, name, arg, n, false))
                      else NONE)
           else if name = ";" then repeatFind (api, st, false, n)
           else if name = "," then repeatFind (api, st, true, n)
           else if name = "%"
                then (case cnt of
                           NONE   => Motions.matchBracket (api, st)
                         | SOME p => SOME (nonBlank (api, st, (p * (last + 1) + 99) div 100 - 1)))
           else if name = "{" then Motions.paragraphBack (api, st, n)
           else if name = "}" then Motions.paragraphForward (api, st, n)
           else if name = "gg" then SOME (nonBlank (api, st, n - 1))
           else if name = "G"  then SOME (nonBlank (api, st, case cnt of NONE => last | SOME p => p - 1))
           else if name = "H"  then SOME (nonBlank (api, st, st.top + n - 1))
           else if name = "L"  then SOME (nonBlank (api, st, st.top + h - n))
           else if name = "M"
                then let val bottom = if st.top + h - 1 > last then last else st.top + h - 1
                     in SOME (nonBlank (api, st, (st.top + bottom) div 2))
                     end
           else if name = "+" orelse name = "<enter>"
                then Option.map (fn s => nonBlank (api, s, s.line)) (byLines (api, st, n))
           else if name = "-"
                then Option.map (fn s => nonBlank (api, s, s.line)) (byLines (api, st, 0 - n))
           else if name = "_"  then SOME (nonBlank (api, st, st.line + n - 1))
           else if name = "n" orelse name = "N"
                then (if st.find = "" then NONE
                      else Motions.search (api, st, st.find, st.findWord,
                                           if name = "n" then st.findDown else not st.findDown, n))
           else if name = "*" orelse name = "#"
                then (case Motions.wordUnder (api, st) of
                           NONE => NONE
                         | SOME (w, c) =>
                             let val st1 = api.setFind (api.moveTo (st, st.line, c), w, name = "*", true)
                             in Motions.search (api, st1, w, true, name = "*", n)
                             end)
           else if name = "'" orelse name = "`"
                then (case api.markAt (st, if arg = "'" orelse arg = "`" then "'" else arg) of
                           NONE => NONE
                         | SOME (l, c) => SOME (if name = "'" then nonBlank (api, st, l)
                                                else api.moveTo (st, l, c)))
           else if name = "<c-f>" orelse name = "<pgdn>" then byLines (api, st, n * h)
           else if name = "<c-b>" orelse name = "<pgup>" then byLines (api, st, 0 - n * h)
           else if name = "<c-d>" then byLines (api, st, n * (h div 2))
           else if name = "<c-u>" then byLines (api, st, 0 - n * (h div 2))
           else NONE
        end

    (** A motion as a command: the cursor moved, a jump remembered, a failed search reported. *)
    fun moveCmd (api, st, name, arg, cnt) =
        case move (api, st, name, arg, cnt, false) of
             SOME s => SOME (if isJump name then api.setMark (s, "'", st.line, st.col) else s, false)
           | NONE   =>
               if (name = "n" orelse name = "N") andalso st.find = ""
               then SOME (api.setStatus (st, noPatternMessage), false)
               else if name = "n" orelse name = "N"
               then SOME (api.setStatus (st, Motions.notFoundMessage st.find), false)
               else if name = "*" orelse name = "#"
               then (case Motions.wordUnder (api, st) of
                          SOME (w, _) => SOME (api.setStatus (st, Motions.notFoundMessage w), false)
                        | NONE        => NONE)
               else if name = "'" orelse name = "`"
               then SOME (api.setStatus (st, noMarkMessage), false)
               else NONE

    (*----------------------------------  Operators  ----------------------------------*)

    (** The span an operator's target covers, or NONE. `cw` on a word changes to its end. *)
    fun spanFor (api, st, op, target, cnt) =
        let val n = Option.getOrElse cnt 1
            val last = api.lastLine st
        in case target of
                SAME => SOME (st.line, if st.line + n - 1 > last then last else st.line + n - 1, true)
              | OBJECT (kind, ch) =>
                  let val around = kind = "a"
                  in if ch = "w" orelse ch = "W" then TextObjects.word (api, st, n, ch = "W", around)
                     else if ch = "p" then TextObjects.paragraph (api, st, n, around)
                     else if ch = "(" orelse ch = ")" orelse ch = "b"
                          then TextObjects.bracket (api, st, n, "(", around)
                     else if ch = "[" orelse ch = "]" then TextObjects.bracket (api, st, n, "[", around)
                     else if ch = "{" orelse ch = "}" orelse ch = "B"
                          then TextObjects.bracket (api, st, n, "{", around)
                     else if ch = "<" orelse ch = ">" then TextObjects.bracket (api, st, n, "<", around)
                     else TextObjects.quote (api, st, ch, around)
                  end
              | MOTION (name, arg) =>
                  let val line = api.lineAt (st, st.line)
                      val len  = String.size line
                      val cls  = if name = "W" then Motions.bigClassOf else Motions.classOf
                      val onWord = st.col < len andalso cls (String.sub (line, st.col)) <> Motions.classSpace
                      val atEnd  = onWord andalso (st.col + 1 >= len
                                                   orelse cls (String.sub (line, st.col + 1))
                                                          <> cls (String.sub (line, st.col)))
                  in if op = "c" andalso (name = "w" orelse name = "W") andalso onWord
                     then (if atEnd andalso n = 1
                           then SOME (Operators.spanOf (api, st, st.line, st.col, INCLUSIVE))
                           else Option.map (fn s => Operators.spanOf (api, st, s.line, s.col, INCLUSIVE))
                                           (Motions.wordEnd (api, st, if atEnd then n - 1 else n, name = "W")))
                     else Option.map (fn s => Operators.spanOf (api, st, s.line, s.col, kindOf (name, st)))
                                     (move (api, st, name, arg, cnt, true))
                  end
        end

    (** The operator applied to its span. `c` enters insert mode, the session having been begun
     *  by the caller. *)
    fun operate (api, st, op, target, cnt) =
        case spanFor (api, st, op, target, cnt) of
             NONE => NONE
           | SOME span =>
               SOME (if op = "d" then Operators.delete (api, st, span)
                     else if op = "c" then api.setMode (Operators.change (api, st, span), INSERT)
                     else if op = "y" then Operators.yank (api, st, span)
                     else if op = ">" then Operators.shift (api, st, span, true)
                     else if op = "<" then Operators.shift (api, st, span, false)
                     else Operators.recase (api, st, span, String.substring (op, 1, 2)))

    (*----------------------------------  Commands  -----------------------------------*)

    fun timesOr (n, f, st) = let fun go (k, s) = if k <= 0 then s else go (k - 1, f s) in go (n, st) end

    (** The shorthand commands as the operator commands they stand for. *)
    fun shorthand "x"     = SOME ("d", MOTION ("l", ""))
      | shorthand "<del>" = SOME ("d", MOTION ("l", ""))
      | shorthand "X"     = SOME ("d", MOTION ("h", ""))
      | shorthand "D"     = SOME ("d", MOTION ("$", ""))
      | shorthand "C"     = SOME ("c", MOTION ("$", ""))
      | shorthand "s"     = SOME ("c", MOTION ("l", ""))
      | shorthand "S"     = SOME ("c", SAME)
      | shorthand "Y"     = SOME ("y", SAME)
      | shorthand _       = NONE

    (** A command that stands alone: SOME (state', quit) or NONE when it could not be done. The
     *  insert commands only place the cursor and set the mode; the session was begun by the
     *  caller. *)
    fun act (api, commands, st, name, arg, cnt) =
        let val n = Option.getOrElse cnt 1
            val len = api.lineLength (st, st.line)
            val h = api.textRows st
            fun ok s = SOME (s, false)
            fun okOpt r = Option.map (fn s => (s, false)) r
        in case shorthand name of
                SOME (op, target) => okOpt (operate (api, st, op, target, cnt))
              | NONE =>
                     if name = "p" then ok (Operators.put (api, st, n, true))
                else if name = "P" then ok (Operators.put (api, st, n, false))
                else if name = "J" then ok (Operators.join (api, st, n, true))
                else if name = "gJ" then ok (Operators.join (api, st, n, false))
                else if name = "r"
                     then (if arg = "<enter>" then okOpt (Operators.replaceChars (api, st, n, "\n"))
                           else if isPrintable arg then okOpt (Operators.replaceChars (api, st, n, arg))
                           else NONE)
                else if name = "~" then ok (Operators.toggleCase (api, st, n))
                else if name = "u" then ok (timesOr (n, api.undo, st))
                else if name = "<c-r>" then ok (timesOr (n, api.redo, st))
                else if name = "i" then ok (api.setMode (st, INSERT))
                else if name = "a"
                     then ok (api.setMode (api.moveTo (st, st.line, if st.col < len then st.col + 1 else st.col), INSERT))
                else if name = "I" then ok (api.setMode (nonBlank (api, st, st.line), INSERT))
                else if name = "A" then ok (api.setMode (api.moveEnd (st, st.line), INSERT))
                else if name = "o" then ok (api.setMode (Operators.openLine (api, st, false), INSERT))
                else if name = "O" then ok (api.setMode (Operators.openLine (api, st, true), INSERT))
                else if name = "R" then ok (api.setMode (st, REPLACE))
                else if name = "v" then ok (api.setMode (api.setAnchor (st, st.line, st.col), VISUAL))
                else if name = "V" then ok (api.setMode (api.setAnchor (st, st.line, st.col), VLINE))
                else if name = "m"
                     then (if isLetter arg then ok (api.setMark (st, arg, st.line, st.col)) else NONE)
                else if name = "zz" then ok (api.setTop (st, st.line - h div 2))
                else if name = "zt" then ok (api.setTop (st, st.line))
                else if name = "zb" then ok (api.setTop (st, st.line - h + 1))
                else if name = "<c-e>" then ok (api.setTop (st, st.top + n))
                else if name = "<c-y>" then ok (api.setTop (st, st.top - n))
                else if name = "ZZ" then SOME (commands (st, "wq"))
                else if name = "ZQ" then SOME (commands (st, "q!"))
                else if name = "q" orelse name = "<c-c>" then SOME (commands (st, "q"))
                else if name = ":" orelse name = "/" orelse name = "?" then ok (api.openPrompt (st, name))
                else if name = "<esc>" then ok st
                else moveCmd (api, st, name, arg, cnt)
        end

    (*-----------------------------  Running a command  -------------------------------*)

    (** Whether a command changes the buffer, and so is what `.` repeats. *)
    fun isChange (OPERATE (_, op, _)) = op <> "y"
      | isChange (ACT (_, name, _)) =
          List.elem name ["x", "<del>", "X", "s", "S", "D", "C", "p", "P", "J", "gJ", "r", "~"
                         , "i", "a", "I", "A", "o", "O", "R"]

    (** The mode a command opens, if it opens one, and the count that insert carries. *)
    fun opensMode (OPERATE (_, op, _)) = if op = "c" then SOME (INSERT, 1) else NONE
      | opensMode (ACT (cnt, name, _)) =
          if List.elem name ["s", "S", "C"] then SOME (INSERT, 1)
          else if List.elem name ["i", "a", "I", "A", "o", "O"] then SOME (INSERT, Option.getOrElse cnt 1)
          else if name = "R" then SOME (REPLACE, Option.getOrElse cnt 1)
          else NONE

    fun execute (api, commands, st, OPERATE (cnt, op, target)) =
          Option.map (fn s => (s, false)) (operate (api, st, op, target, cnt))
      | execute (api, commands, st, ACT (cnt, name, arg)) = act (api, commands, st, name, arg, cnt)

    (** A complete command run against `st`, whose pending is already cleared: the insert session
     *  begun first when the command opens one, the change recorded for `.`, the undo entries it
     *  pushed squashed into one, and the cursor pulled onto the line. A command that could not be
     *  done leaves the state as it was. *)
    fun run (api, commands, st, cmd, toks) =
        let val depth = api.undoDepth st
            val st0 = case opensMode cmd of
                           SOME (m, n) => api.beginInsert (st, m, n)
                         | NONE        => st
        in case execute (api, commands, st0, cmd) of
                NONE => (st, false)
              | SOME (st1, quit) =>
                  let val st2 = if isChange cmd then api.setDot (st1, toks, []) else st1
                  in case st2.mode of
                          NORMAL => (api.intoLine (api.squashUndo (st2, depth)), quit)
                        | _      => (st2, quit)
                  end
        end

    (** The tokens with their count replaced by `cnt`, when one is given. *)
    fun recount (toks, cnt) =
        let val (_, rest) = count toks
        in case cnt of
                NONE   => toks
              | SOME n => List.append (tokensOf (toString n)) rest
        end

    (** The tokens without their count. *)
    fun uncount toks = let val (_, rest) = count toks in rest end

    (*--------------------------------  Insert mode  ---------------------------------*)

    (** The column where CTRL-w's deletion starts: the start of the word before the cursor on
     *  its line, the spaces before the cursor stepped over first. *)
    fun wordStartBefore (api, st) =
        let val line = api.lineAt (st, st.line)
            fun skipSpace i = if i > 0 andalso Motions.isSpace (String.sub (line, i - 1)) then skipSpace (i - 1) else i
            val i = skipSpace st.col
        in if i = 0 then 0
           else let val k = Motions.classOf (String.sub (line, i - 1))
                    fun back j = if j > 0 andalso Motions.classOf (String.sub (line, j - 1)) = k
                                 then back (j - 1) else j
                in back i
                end
        end

    (** How many code units CTRL-d takes off the front of the line: one tab, or up to eight
     *  spaces. *)
    fun dedentUnits (api, st) =
        let val line = api.lineAt (st, st.line)
            val n = String.size line
        in if n > 0 andalso String.sub (line, 0) = "\t" then 1
           else let fun spaces i = if i < n andalso i < 8 andalso String.sub (line, i) = " "
                                   then spaces (i + 1) else i
                in spaces 0
                end
        end

    (** One token in insert or replace mode, other than the one that leaves it. *)
    fun insertToken (api, st0, tok) =
        let val st = api.noteTyped (st0, tok)
            val replacing = case st.mode of REPLACE => true | _ => false
        in      if tok = "<enter>" then api.insertText (st, "\n")
           else if tok = "<tab>" then (if replacing then api.replaceChar (st, "\t") else api.insertText (st, "\t"))
           else if tok = "<bs>"
                then (if replacing
                      then (if api.undoDepth st > st.insertMark then api.undo st
                            else if st.col > 0 then api.moveTo (st, st.line, st.col - 1) else st)
                      else api.backspace st)
           else if tok = "<del>" then api.deleteChar st
           else if tok = "<c-w>"
                then (if st.col = 0 then api.backspace st
                      else let val c = wordStartBefore (api, st)
                           in api.deleteAt (st, api.lineStart (st, st.line) + c, st.col - c)
                           end)
           else if tok = "<c-u>"
                then (if st.col = 0 then st
                      else api.deleteAt (st, api.lineStart (st, st.line), st.col))
           else if tok = "<c-t>"
                then let val st1 = api.insertAt (st, api.lineStart (st, st.line), "\t")
                     in api.moveTo (st1, st.line, st.col + 1)
                     end
           else if tok = "<c-d>"
                then let val k = dedentUnits (api, st)
                         val st1 = api.deleteAt (st, api.lineStart (st, st.line), k)
                     in api.moveTo (st1, st.line, if st.col > k then st.col - k else 0)
                     end
           else if isPrintable tok then (if replacing then api.replaceChar (st, tok) else api.insertText (st, tok))
           else if tok = "<left>" then api.moveTo (st, st.line, st.col - 1)
           else if tok = "<right>" then api.moveTo (st, st.line, st.col + 1)
           else if tok = "<up>" then api.moveLine (st, st.line - 1)
           else if tok = "<down>" then api.moveLine (st, st.line + 1)
           else if tok = "<home>" then api.moveTo (st, st.line, 0)
           else if tok = "<end>" then api.moveEnd (st, st.line)
           else if tok = "<pgdn>" then api.moveLine (st, st.line + api.textRows st)
           else if tok = "<pgup>" then api.moveLine (st, st.line - api.textRows st)
           else st
        end

    fun feedInsert (api, st, keys) = List.foldl (fn (k, s) => insertToken (api, s, k)) st keys

    (** The session ended without any count: normal mode, one undo step, the cursor stepped
     *  left onto the last character typed. *)
    fun finishInsert (api, st) =
        let val st1 = api.endInsert st
        in api.intoLine (if st1.col > 0 then api.moveTo (st1, st1.line, st1.col - 1) else st1)
        end

    (** Whether the change that opened the insert was `o` or `O`, whose count repeats the whole
     *  command rather than the typed keys alone. *)
    fun opensLine toks = case parse toks of
                              DONE (ACT (_, name, _)) => name = "o" orelse name = "O"
                            | _ => false

    (** Esc in insert or replace mode: the typed keys repeated for the count the insert was
     *  entered with, then the session ended. The repeats' own sessions are squashed into the
     *  first, so `3ohi` is one undo step. *)
    fun leaveInsert (api, commands, st) =
        let val keys  = List.reverse st.typed
            val n     = st.insertCount
            val mark  = st.insertMark
            val toks  = uncount st.dot
            fun again s =
                if opensLine toks
                then let val (s1, _) = case parse toks of
                                            DONE cmd => run (api, commands, finishInsert (api, s), cmd, toks)
                                          | _        => (s, false)
                     in feedInsert (api, s1, keys)
                     end
                else feedInsert (api, s, keys)
            val st1 = timesOr (n - 1, again, st)
            val st2 = finishInsert (api, st1)
            val st3 = if mark >= 0 then api.squashUndo (st2, mark) else st2
        in api.setDot (st3, st.dot, keys)
        end

    (*--------------------------------  Repeating  -----------------------------------*)

    (** `.`: the last change's tokens run again, its typed keys fed again, and its insert ended
     *  — as one undo step. *)
    fun repeatChange (api, commands, st, cnt) =
        if st.dot = [] then (api.setStatus (st, noChangeMessage), false)
        else let val toks = recount (st.dot, cnt)
                 val keys = st.dotInsert
             in case parse toks of
                     DONE cmd =>
                       let val (st1, quit) = run (api, commands, st, cmd, toks)
                       in case st1.mode of
                               NORMAL => (st1, quit)
                             | _      => (leaveInsert (api, commands, feedInsert (api, st1, keys)), quit)
                       end
                   | _ => (st, false)
             end

    (*--------------------------------  Normal mode  ---------------------------------*)

    (** One token in normal mode: the pending command extended by it and parsed. *)
    fun normalToken (api, commands, st, tok) =
        let val toks = List.append (tokensOf st.pending) [tok]
            val cleared = api.setPending (st, "")
        in if tok = "<esc>" then (cleared, false)
           else case parse toks of
                     MORE     => (api.setPending (st, st.pending ^ tok), false)
                   | BAD      => (cleared, false)
                   | DONE cmd =>
                       (case cmd of
                             ACT (cnt, ".", _) => repeatChange (api, commands, cleared, cnt)
                           | _                 => run (api, commands, cleared, cmd, toks))
        end

    (*--------------------------------  Command mode  --------------------------------*)

    (** The pattern typed at a search prompt, remembered and run in the prompt's direction. An
     *  empty pattern repeats the last one, as vi's does. A hit is a jump. *)
    fun runSearch (api, st, pat, down) =
        let val pattern = if pat = "" then st.find else pat
        in if pattern = "" then api.setStatus (st, noPatternMessage)
           else let val st1 = api.setFind (st, pattern, down, false)
                in case Motions.search (api, st1, pattern, false, down, 1) of
                        SOME s => api.setMark (s, "'", st.line, st.col)
                      | NONE   => api.setStatus (st1, Motions.notFoundMessage pattern)
                end
        end

    (** What Enter does with the line is what the prompt says: a command word goes to the command
     *  interpreter, a search pattern to the search above. *)
    fun runPrompt (api, commands, st, prompt, line) =
        if prompt = ":" then commands (st, line)
        else (api.intoLine (runSearch (api, st, line, prompt = "/")), false)

    fun commandToken (api, commands, st, tok) =
             if tok = "<enter>" then runPrompt (api, commands, api.closePrompt st, st.prompt, st.cmd)
        else if tok = "<esc>" orelse tok = "<c-c>" then (api.closePrompt st, false)
        else if tok = "<bs>"
             then (if st.cmd = "" then (api.closePrompt st, false)
                   else (api.setCmd (st, String.substring (st.cmd, 0, String.size st.cmd - 1)), false))
        else if tok = "<c-u>" then (api.setCmd (st, ""), false)
        else if isPrintable tok then (api.setCmd (st, st.cmd ^ tok), false)
        else (st, false)

    (*---------------------------------  Visual mode  ---------------------------------*)

    (** The keys that act on a selection. *)
    fun isVisualAct t =
        List.elem t [ "d", "x", "<del>", "X", "D", "c", "s", "C", "S", "R", "y", "Y", "<", ">"
                    , "~", "u", "U", "J", "p", "P", "o", "v", "V", "<esc>", "<c-c>"
                    , "<c-e>", "<c-y>" ]

    (** The tokens as a visual-mode command: a count, then a motion, an object, a key that acts
     *  on the selection, or one of the two-key sequences. *)
    fun parseVisual toks =
        let val (n, rest) = count toks
        in case rest of
                []        => MORE
              | t :: more =>
                  if t = "g"
                  then (case more of
                             []     => MORE
                           | u :: _ => if List.elem u ["J", "u", "U", "~", "g", "e", "E"]
                                       then DONE (ACT (n, "g" ^ u, "")) else BAD)
                  else if t = "i" orelse t = "a"
                  then (case more of
                             []     => MORE
                           | u :: _ => if isObjectChar u then DONE (ACT (n, t, u)) else BAD)
                  else if needsChar t orelse t = "r" orelse t = "m"
                  then (case more of
                             []     => MORE
                           | u :: _ => DONE (ACT (n, t, u)))
                  else if t = "z"
                  then (case more of
                             []     => MORE
                           | u :: _ => if u = "z" orelse u = "t" orelse u = "b"
                                       then DONE (ACT (n, "z" ^ u, "")) else BAD)
                  else if isMotion t orelse isVisualAct t then DONE (ACT (n, t, ""))
                  else BAD
        end

    (** The span between the anchor and the cursor: whole lines in linewise mode, otherwise the
     *  characters from the one to the other, both included. `linewise` forces the lines. *)
    fun selection (api, st, linewise) =
        let val (al, ac) = st.anchor
            val kind = case st.mode of VLINE => LINEWISE | _ => if linewise then LINEWISE else INCLUSIVE
        in Operators.spanOf (api, st, al, ac, kind)
        end

    fun leaveVisual (api, st) = api.intoLine (api.setMode (st, NORMAL))

    (** The selection replaced by the register (charwise: put before the start of what was
     *  deleted), or an operator applied to it. Each ends the selection. *)
    fun visualOp (api, st, op, linewise) =
        let val span = selection (api, st, linewise)
        in      if op = "d" then leaveVisual (api, Operators.delete (api, st, span))
           else if op = "y" then leaveVisual (api, Operators.yank (api, st, span))
           else if op = "c" then api.setMode (Operators.change (api, st, span), INSERT)
           else if op = ">" then leaveVisual (api, Operators.shift (api, st, span, true))
           else if op = "<" then leaveVisual (api, Operators.shift (api, st, span, false))
           else if op = "p" then leaveVisual (api, Operators.putOver (api, st, span))
           else leaveVisual (api, Operators.recase (api, st, span, op))
        end

    (** An object in visual mode: the selection becomes the object, the anchor at its start and
     *  the cursor on its last character, linewise for a paragraph. *)
    fun selectObject (api, st, kind, ch, cnt) =
        case spanFor (api, st, "y", OBJECT (kind, ch), cnt) of
             NONE => NONE
           | SOME (l1, l2, true) =>
               SOME (api.moveTo (api.setMode (api.setAnchor (st, l1, 0), VLINE), l2, 0))
           | SOME (a, b, false) =>
               let val (al, ac) = Operators.positionOf (api, st, a)
                   val (cl, cc) = Operators.positionOf (api, st, if b > a then b - 1 else a)
               in SOME (api.moveTo (api.setMode (api.setAnchor (st, al, ac), VISUAL), cl, cc))
               end

    (** One command in visual mode: SOME (state', quit) or NONE. *)
    fun visualAct (api, commands, st, name, arg, cnt) =
        let val n = Option.getOrElse cnt 1
            val h = api.textRows st
            val (al, ac) = st.anchor
            val (l1, l2) = case selection (api, st, true) of (a, b, _) => (a, b)
            fun ok s = SOME (s, false)
            fun linewiseChange s = api.setMode (Operators.change (api, s, selection (api, s, true)), INSERT)
        in      if name = "d" orelse name = "x" orelse name = "<del>" then ok (visualOp (api, st, "d", false))
           else if name = "X" orelse name = "D" then ok (visualOp (api, st, "d", true))
           else if name = "y" then ok (visualOp (api, st, "y", false))
           else if name = "Y" then ok (visualOp (api, st, "y", true))
           else if name = "c" orelse name = "s" then ok (visualOp (api, st, "c", false))
           else if name = "C" orelse name = "S" orelse name = "R" then ok (linewiseChange st)
           else if name = ">" orelse name = "<"
                then ok (leaveVisual (api, timesOr (n, fn s => Operators.shift (api, s, selection (api, st, false), name = ">"), st)))
           else if name = "~" orelse name = "g~" then ok (visualOp (api, st, "~", false))
           else if name = "u" orelse name = "gu" then ok (visualOp (api, st, "u", false))
           else if name = "U" orelse name = "gU" then ok (visualOp (api, st, "U", false))
           else if name = "J" orelse name = "gJ"
                then ok (leaveVisual (api, Operators.join (api, api.moveTo (st, l1, 0), l2 - l1 + 1, name = "J")))
           else if name = "p" orelse name = "P" then ok (visualOp (api, st, "p", false))
           else if name = "r"
                then (if isPrintable arg
                      then ok (leaveVisual (api, Operators.fill (api, st, selection (api, st, false), arg)))
                      else NONE)
           else if name = "o" then ok (api.moveTo (api.setAnchor (st, st.line, st.col), al, ac))
           else if name = "v"
                then ok (case st.mode of VISUAL => leaveVisual (api, st) | _ => api.setMode (st, VISUAL))
           else if name = "V"
                then ok (case st.mode of VLINE => leaveVisual (api, st) | _ => api.setMode (st, VLINE))
           else if name = "<esc>" orelse name = "<c-c>" then ok (leaveVisual (api, st))
           else if name = "i" orelse name = "a"
                then Option.map (fn s => (s, false)) (selectObject (api, st, name, arg, cnt))
           else if name = "m"
                then (if isLetter arg then ok (api.setMark (st, arg, st.line, st.col)) else NONE)
           else if name = "zz" then ok (api.setTop (st, st.line - h div 2))
           else if name = "zt" then ok (api.setTop (st, st.line))
           else if name = "zb" then ok (api.setTop (st, st.line - h + 1))
           else if name = "<c-e>" then ok (api.setTop (st, st.top + n))
           else if name = "<c-y>" then ok (api.setTop (st, st.top - n))
           else moveCmd (api, st, name, arg, cnt)
        end

    (** One token in visual mode: the pending command extended and parsed, as in normal mode.
     *  A command that ends the selection with an edit is one undo step; a change that opens an
     *  insert is not what `.` repeats. *)
    fun visualToken (api, commands, st, tok) =
        let val toks = List.append (tokensOf st.pending) [tok]
            val cleared = api.setPending (st, "")
        in case parseVisual toks of
                MORE     => (api.setPending (st, st.pending ^ tok), false)
              | BAD      => (cleared, false)
              | DONE (ACT (cnt, name, arg)) =>
                  let val depth = api.undoDepth st
                      val st0 = if List.elem name ["c", "s", "C", "S", "R"]
                                then api.setDot (api.beginInsert (cleared, INSERT, 1), [], [])
                                else cleared
                  in case visualAct (api, commands, st0, name, arg, cnt) of
                          NONE => (cleared, false)
                        | SOME (st1, quit) =>
                            (case st1.mode of
                                  NORMAL => (api.intoLine (api.squashUndo (st1, depth)), quit)
                                | _      => (st1, quit))
                  end
              | DONE _ => (cleared, false)
        end

    (*----------------------------------  Help mode  ---------------------------------*)

    (** Space, PageDown, `j` and Down turn to the next page, `b`, PageUp, `k` and Up to the one
     *  before; any other key puts the page away and the buffer back, the key spent on that. *)
    fun helpToken (api, helpPages, st, tok) =
        let val last = helpPages st - 1
        in if tok = " " orelse tok = "<pgdn>" orelse tok = "j" orelse tok = "<down>"
           then (api.setHelpPage (st, if st.helpPage >= last then last else st.helpPage + 1), false)
           else if tok = "b" orelse tok = "<pgup>" orelse tok = "k" orelse tok = "<up>"
           then (api.setHelpPage (st, if st.helpPage <= 0 then 0 else st.helpPage - 1), false)
           else (api.setHelpPage (api.setMode (st, NORMAL), 0), false)
        end

    (*-----------------------------------  The map  ----------------------------------*)

    (** `(state', quit)` for one key.
     *
     *  A transient status message is cleared here rather than where it is set, so every message
     *  is shown for exactly as long as it takes the user to press the next key. *)
    fun onKey (api, commands, helpPages, st0, k) =
        let val st  = if st0.status = "" then st0 else api.setStatus (st0, "")
            val tok = tokenOf k
            fun typing () = if tok = "<esc>" orelse tok = "<c-c>" then (leaveInsert (api, commands, st), false)
                            else (insertToken (api, st, tok), false)
        in case st.mode of
                INSERT  => typing ()
              | REPLACE => typing ()
              | VISUAL  => visualToken (api, commands, st, tok)
              | VLINE   => visualToken (api, commands, st, tok)
              | COMMAND => commandToken (api, commands, st, tok)
              | HELP    => helpToken (api, helpPages, st, tok)
              | NORMAL  => normalToken (api, commands, st, tok)
        end

    (*----------------------------------  The help  ----------------------------------*)

    (** What `:help` says about this keymap: the sections the plugin set assembles the help page
     *  from (Help.trp). A key added above belongs in the section it belongs to here. A function
     *  rather than a value because a double quote cannot be written inside a string literal. *)
    fun help () =
        let val dq = String.strCode 34
        in
        [ ("MOTION",
           [ ("h j k l",   "move by one; arrows too")
           , ("w b e",     "next word, back, word end")
           , ("W B E",     "the same over blank-delimited words")
           , ("ge gE",     "back to a word end")
           , ("0 ^ $ |",   "line start, first non-blank, end, column")
           , ("f t F T",   "to or till a character, back with F T")
           , ("; ,",       "repeat the find, reversed")
           , ("%",         "matching bracket")
           , ("{ }",       "paragraph back, forward")
           , ("gg G",      "first line, last or line N")
           , ("H M L",     "screen top, middle, bottom")
           , ("+ - Enter", "line down, up, to first non-blank")
           , ("^F ^B",     "page down, up; PgDn PgUp too")
           , ("^D ^U",     "half a page down, up")
           , ("^E ^Y",     "scroll a line down, up")
           , ("zz zt zb",  "cursor line to middle, top, bottom") ])
        , ("OPERATOR",
           [ ("d c y",     "delete, change, yank a motion")
           , ("< >",       "shift lines left, right")
           , ("g~ gu gU",  "toggle, lower, upper case")
           , ("dd cc yy",  "the line; >> << gUU likewise")
           , ("N before",  "a count on any of these") ])
        , ("OBJECT",
           [ ("iw aw",     "a word, with its spaces")
           , ("iW aW",     "a blank-delimited word")
           , ("i( a( ib",  "inside, around ( ); [ { < too")
           , ("i" ^ dq ^ " i' i`", "inside quotes; a for around")
           , ("ip ap",     "a paragraph") ])
        , ("EDIT",
           [ ("i a I A",   "insert here, after, at start, end")
           , ("o O",       "open a line below, above")
           , ("R",         "replace mode until Esc")
           , ("x X",       "delete under, before the cursor")
           , ("s S",       "change a character, the line")
           , ("D C Y",     "to the end of the line; Y yanks the line")
           , ("r",         "replace one character")
           , ("~",         "toggle case and move on")
           , ("J gJ",      "join lines, without a space")
           , ("p P",       "put after, before")
           , ("u ^R",      "undo, redo")
           , (".",         "repeat the last change")
           , ("Esc",       "leave insert or replace mode") ])
        , ("INSERT",
           [ ("^W ^U",     "delete a word, the line before the cursor")
           , ("^T ^D",     "indent, dedent the line")
           , ("Enter Tab", "line break, tab") ])
        , ("SEARCH",
           [ ("/text",     "search forward; ?text back")
           , ("n N",       "next, previous match")
           , ("* #",       "the word under the cursor, forward, back") ])
        , ("MARK",
           [ ("ma",        "set mark a")
           , ("'a `a",     "go to its line, its column")
           , ("'' ``",     "back before the last jump") ])
        , ("SESSION",
           [ (":",         "start a command")
           , ("ZZ ZQ",     "write and quit; quit discarding")
           , ("q ^C",      "quit like :q") ])
        ]
        end

in [ ("onKey", onKey)
   , ("help", help)
   ]
end
